"\\:py\\:obj\\:\\`None\\``"
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:1 of
msgid "Compute all intersection points of two arbitrary VMobjects."
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:3 of
msgid ""
"Every :class:`~manim.mobject.types.vectorized_mobject.VMobject` stores "
"its outline as a sequence of cubic Bézier curves, so this function treats"
" the two inputs uniformly as families of cubic Bézier curves and "
"intersects them *without* any type-specific special cases.  The algorithm"
" is:"
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:8 of
msgid ""
"the Bézier tree of each mobject (including submobjects) is collected, "
"skipping ``NaN`` path-break markers;"
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:10 of
msgid ""
"each curve pair is recursively subdivided with de Casteljau's algorithm, "
"always splitting the less flat curve;"
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:12 of
msgid ""
"pairs whose control-point bounding boxes do not overlap are pruned "
"immediately — a Bézier curve is always contained in the convex hull (and "
"hence the bounding box) of its control points, so this never discards a "
"real intersection;"
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:16 of
msgid ""
"once both sub-curves deviate from their chords by less than *flatness*, "
"they are treated as line segments and a closest-point test (with a "
"distance tolerance accounting for the approximation error) decides "
"whether the true curves meet;"
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:20 of
msgid ""
"coincident, overlapping curve pieces report the endpoints of their common"
" interval instead of infinitely many points."
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:23 of
msgid ""
"Tangencies, crossings at curve joins and intersections in 3-D are all "
"handled by the same subdivision loop.  When the same mobject is passed "
"for both arguments the function reports its self-intersections (shared "
"path-join anchors are filtered out)."
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:28 of
msgid "The first vectorised mobject."
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:30 of
msgid "The second vectorised mobject."
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:32 of
msgid ""
"Distance below which two points are considered the same intersection, and"
" the base acceptance distance for the flat segment closest-point test."
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:36 of
msgid ""
"Maximum allowed deviation of a Bézier sub-curve's control points from its"
" chord before the sub-curve is treated as a straight segment.  Smaller "
"values yield more accurate intersection points at the cost of more "
"subdivision."
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:41 of
msgid ""
"Maximum number of recursive subdivision levels.  Guarantees termination "
"for pathological configurations such as tangencies."
msgstr ""

#: manim_extensions.geometry.VMobjectInt:45 of
msgid ""
"All intersection points as 3-D arrays.  An empty list is returned when "
"the mobjects do not meet.  If the two outlines overlap along a curve "
"segment, the endpoints of the overlapping region are returned."
msgstr ""

